# Apache has no default MIME mapping for .mjs, so browsers refuse to run
# the pdf.js ES module (strict MIME checking on <script type="module"> and
# dynamic import()). This is Apache-only — nginx (the production TU/e
# server) needs the equivalent added to its server config when this is
# deployed there: `types { text/javascript mjs; }` in the relevant
# location block, or a line in nginx's mime.types.
AddType text/javascript .mjs
